# Gallivm is intentionally retired from the AROS target build.
#
# The declaration introduced in 2019 never had an active consumer: its only
# aggregate edge and LLVM feature define were disabled from the start, while
# mesa3dgl.library links the ordinary Gallium archive instead. Mesa 20.0.8's
# Gallivm sources require target-side LLVM headers plus the LLVM Core,
# ExecutionEngine and MCJIT runtimes; the current x86, ARM and AArch64 SDKs
# provide none of those. The repository's LLVM toolchain is host-only.
#
# Reintroducing Gallivm is therefore a new porting feature, not restoration of
# a working legacy target. It must arrive with a target LLVM runtime, an active
# consumer and architecture runtime tests rather than an empty archive.
